      "problem": "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. $A$ has a zero column\n\nII. $A$ has two proportional rows\n\nIII. One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$",
