      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/a5ccddc0640f27c28b4469fa3e9dc6debf4e5216c67f6bc49f894e26eac6c748.svg)\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/138737153bd4bd877ed9a5e8cb0d60be7bcb66587bdcb1e750e62c3277de1dbc.svg)\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
